Dataset
The dataset used in this study is the Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset (Olist), available on Kaggle. It contains approximately 100,000 orders distributed across multiple relational tables, including customers, orders, order_items, sellers, payments, products, and reviews. The dataset incorporates foreign-key relationships, transactional lifecycle timestamps, monetary attributes, and categorical workflow states. Its multi-table relational schema and referential dependencies reflect realistic transactional structures commonly observed in enterprise systems. The presence of lifecycle events and inter-table relationships makes it suitable for evaluating relational integrity and workflow consistency in synthetic data generation. Overall, the dataset provides a practical approximation of Salesforce-like CRM object relationships and operational transitions, enabling controlled experimentation on constraint-aware relational synthetic data modelling.
Dataset Link: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce
